l, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15894, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QnZ4Losf1HGLBvrDWbM3vP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18474, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0147RUntv4rRBBjy7LjGUxkf", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy. The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0, so I rolled back to it in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial_failure), leaving the fleet mixed (us-east on v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed and verified.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 49074, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0147RUntv4rRBBjy7LjGUxkf", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 49074, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0147RUntv4rRBBjy7LjGUxkf", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 50301, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_018USQf9owmQ54DzLLExh8GX", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 50601, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018USQf9owmQ54DzLLExh8GX", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 50601, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018USQf9owmQ54DzLLExh8GX", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 52600, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy there, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback once, and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** The SEV2 incident request timed out, but the incident had been created. I confirmed it is INC-0001, open and SEV2 for checkout-api, and did not create a duplicate. It describes the rollback, the partial failure and the retry.\n\nFollow-ups for the incident: investigate why v2.3.1 fails, and find out why the orchestrator halted the first rollback. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed and verified.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01EhVsF7Wc8tQckkXRvfW63h", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CESURs2zEZJViagdGNed5g", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The latest production release, v2.3.1, is unhealthy. The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0, which has been healthy before, so it doesn't need change-manager approval. I'll roll back to it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Pi1dY8SEPPVk7t99X6FJF5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback reported a partial failure after us-east. I'll check the current state before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HNaZ1YWHgLHbCe3fievrJG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on the unhealthy v2.3.1. The rollback target is the same, so I'll retry it once to finish the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015jNdywkf2wsUkbhdciS2fw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QnZ4Losf1HGLBvrDWbM3vP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "All three regions are on v2.3.0 and healthy again, with error rate down to 0.002. Now I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0147RUntv4rRBBjy7LjGUxkf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy. The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0, so I rolled back to it in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial_failure), leaving the fleet mixed (us-east on v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed and verified.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. I'll check whether it was created before retrying, so I don't open a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018USQf9owmQ54DzLLExh8GX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy there, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the fleet mixed. I retried the same rollback once, and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** The SEV2 incident request timed out, but the incident had been created. I confirmed it is INC-0001, open and SEV2 for checkout-api, and did not create a duplicate. It describes the rollback, the partial failure and the retry.\n\nFollow-ups for the incident: investigate why v2.3.1 fails, and find out why the orchestrator halted the first rollback. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed and verified.", "type": "text"}]}]}